{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And behold, a man of the children of Israel came.</b> The tribe of Shimon gathered around Zimri, for he was their prince. They said to him: We are being condemned to death, and you sit idle! and so on, as is found in Elleh Hen Nisrefin (Sanhedrin 82)." "<b>The Midianite woman.</b> Cozbi daughter of Zur." "<b>In the sight of Moshe.</b> They said to him: Moshe — is this one forbidden or permitted? If you say forbidden — the daughter of Yitro, who permitted her to you? and so on, as is found there." "<b>And they were weeping.</b> The halakhah was hidden from him; they all burst into weeping. At the calf Moshe stood against sixty myriad, as it is said ״וַיִּטְחָן עַד אֲשֶׁר דָּק״ and so on (Exodus 32), and here his hands grew slack? Rather, so that Pinchas would come and take what was coming to him (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:45.144087712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}